{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYTGFbcrpYcM7z4MnDY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenAI published an updated Model Spec on October 29 that reorganizes its public description of model behavior around five values: faithfulness to human intent, harm minimization, honesty and transparency, human agency, and care. Faithfulness is the foundation. OpenAI defines it as understanding what OpenAI, developers and users intend and value, and acting wisely when that understanding is incomplete, which goes past following instructions literally. Its example is a model helping someone compare job offers. It might draw on priorities the person shared earlier, such as predictable hours, while making that assumption visible and easy to correct.\n\nThe update adds a new section on faithfulness that includes a revised chain of command for deciding which instructions apply. It also adds a subsection on how conversations, memories and other context should inform the model's reading of what someone wants. New defaults cover supporting human agency and following relevant social norms, and the guidance on controlling and communicating side effects is expanded. OpenAI is also retiring most of the detailed style guidance. Style is meant to adapt to what people prefer, with user feedback and context as the evidence. Some stronger defaults remain, including approaching questions objectively. The model should not adopt a perspective just because it infers that the user wants to hear it, though users and developers can explicitly ask for one.\n\nMy reading is that removing style rules makes the model's behavior depend more on how well it infers preferences from context. That puts weight on the transparency the Spec asks for, such as stating assumptions so users can correct them.\n\nOpenAI says plainly that its models do not yet fully reflect the Spec. It describes new training methods aimed at teaching the reasons behind the principles, but results will come in later updates. For now the document states a target, and whether organizing around values produces better judgment in situations the rules never covered has yet to be shown."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3682,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3682},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a078e45d-a647-4fa3-9837-d88646382f77","uuid":"ebe18583-1d6d-4804-b906-ee2abf59c771","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:23:55.466Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYTFpHy4ucGrP1umg2f"}
